			</editHistoryEntry>
		</editHistory>
		<skos:definition>The type of position the staff member holds in the specific course section.</skos:definition>
	</rdf:Property>
	<rdf:Property rdf:about="https://w3id.org/CEDStandards/terms/P002073">
		<dc:creator>Common Education Data Standards</dc:creator>
		<dc:identifier rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#token">P002073</dc:identifier>
		<rdfs:label>Has Coding System Organization Type</rdfs:label>
		<schema:domainIncludes rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/CEDStandards/terms/C200178" />
		<schema:rangeIncludes rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/CEDStandards/terms/C002073" />
		<skos:notation>hasCodingSystemOrganizationType</skos:notation>
		<dc:description>The type of organization that created the coding system for this element.</dc:description>
		<textFormat>Option Set</textFormat>
		<editHistory rdf:parseType="Collection"> 
			<editHistoryEntry> 	
				<changeDescription>Added new element to DES.</changeDescription> 	
				<changeVersion>12</changeVersion> 
			</editHistoryEntry>
		</editHistory>
		<skos:definition>The type of organization that created the coding system for this element.</skos:definition>
	</rdf:Property>
	<rdf:Property rdf:about="https://w3id.org/CEDStandards/terms/P000106">
		<dc:creator>Common Education Data Standards</dc:creator>
		<dc:identifier rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#token">P000106</dc:identifier>
		<rdfs:label>Has Cohort Exclusion</rdfs:label>
		<schema:domainIncludes rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/CEDStandards/terms/C200341" />
		<schema:rangeIncludes rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/CEDStandards/terms/C000106" />
		<skos:notation>hasCohortExclusion</skos:notation>
		<dc:description>Those persons who may be removed (deleted) from a cohort (or subcohort). For the Graduation Rates and Fall Enrollment retention rate reporting, persons may be removed from a cohort if they left the institution for one of the following reasons: death or total and permanent disability; service in the armed forces (including those called to active duty); service with a foreign aid service of the federal government, such as the Peace Corps; or service on official church missions.</dc:description>
		<skos:definition>Those persons who may be removed (deleted) from a cohort (or subcohort). For the Graduation Rates and Fall Enrollment retention rate reporting, persons may be removed from a cohort if they left the institution for one of the following reasons: death or total and permanent disability; service in the armed forces (including those called to active duty); service with a foreign aid service of the federal government, such as the Peace Corps; or service on official church missions.</skos:definition>
	</rdf:Property>
	<rdf:Property rdf:about="https://w3id.org/CEDStandards/terms/P001633">
		<dc:creator>Common Education Data Standards</dc:creator>
		<dc:identifier rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#token">P001633</dc:identifier>
		<rdfs:label>Has Community-based Type</rdfs:label>
		<schema:domainIncludes rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/CEDStandards/terms/C200093" />
		<schema:rangeIncludes rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/CEDStandards/terms/C001633" />
		<skos:notation>hasCommunityBasedType</skos:notation>
		<dc:description>Non domestic residence in which the early learning setting is located.</dc:description>
		<skos:definition>Non domestic residence in which the early learning setting is located.</skos:definition>
	</rdf:Property>
	<rdf:Property rdf:about="https://w3id.org/CEDStandards/terms/P000869">
		<dc:creator>Common Education Data Standards</dc:creator>
		<dc:identifier rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#token">P000869</dc:identifier>
		<rdfs:label>Has Competency Association Type</rdfs:label>
		<schema:domainIncludes rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/CEDStandards/terms/C200064" />
		<schema:rangeIncludes rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/CEDStandards/terms/C000869" />
		<skos:notation>hasCompetencyAssociationType</skos:notation>
		<dc:description>Defines the nature of the association between a Competency Definition and an associated data object such as a Learning Resource, an Assessment Item, or even another Competency Definition.</dc:description>
		<rdfs:comment>The Learning Standard Item Association entity defines metadata relationships between a Learning Standard Item and other objects or relationships between Learning Standard Items not otherwise defined in the normal taxonomy of the framework such as for competency-based pathways, relationships between different versions of the same learning standard, and relationships to resources. &lt;br /&gt;&lt;BR/&gt;&lt;BR/&gt;For example, "Prerequisite" may indicate that the Associated Learning Standard Item is a Prerequisite of this Learning Standards Item.  Another association may specify that a Learning Resource "Teaches" the specified Learning Standard Item, or is aligned to the "Reading Level" specified as part of the Learning Standard Item.</rdfs:comment>
		<editHistory rdf:parseType="Collection"> 
			<editHistoryEntry> 	
				<changeDescription>Changes toward common naming throughout the Credentials Ecosystem Mapping community, internal note(definition correction, added space between Learning and Standard)</changeDescription> 	
				<changeVersion>7.1</changeVersion> 
			</editHistoryEntry> 
			<editHistoryEntry> 	
				<changeDescription>Entity name changed from "Competency Item" to "Competency Definition" to support alignment across standards and reduce confusion by those who might think this is a "competency assertion" that is attributed to a person rather than what it is, a definition of a competency that could apply to any person.</changeDescription> 	
				<changeVersion>8</changeVersion> 
			</editHistoryEntry>
		</editHistory>
		<skos:definition>Defines the nature of the association between a Competency Definition and an associated data object such as a Learning Resource, an Assessment Item, or even another Competency Definition.</skos:definition>
	</rdf:Property>
	<rdf:Property rdf:about="https://w3id.org/CEDStandards/terms/P600300">
		<dc:creator>Common Education Data Standards</dc:creator>
		<dc:identifier rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#token">P600300</dc:identifier>
		<rdfs:label>Has Competency Definition Association</rdfs:label>
		<schema:domainIncludes rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/CEDStandards/terms/C200065" />
		<schema:rangeIncludes rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/CEDStandards/terms/C200064" />
		<skos:notation>hasCompetencyDefinitionAssociation</skos:notation>
		<dc:description>References the relation of competency definitions to other competency definitions and/or competency frameworks to competency frameworks to support competency maps or competency sub frameworks or linked controlled vocabulary terms as metadata to further define a competency definition. (In CEDS IDS CompetencyDefAssociation also provides a mechanism to link any other object in the model to a CompetencyDefinition, e.g. to RubricCriterion, LearningResource, Course, or AssessmentItem.)</dc:description>
		<skos:definition>References the relation of competency definitions to other competency definitions and/or competency frameworks to competency frameworks to support competency maps or competency sub frameworks or linked controlled vocabulary terms as metadata to further define a competency definition. (In CEDS IDS CompetencyDefAssociation also provides a mechanism to link any other object in the model to a CompetencyDefinition, e.g. to RubricCriterion, LearningResource, Course, or AssessmentItem.)</skos:definition>
		<editHistory rdf:parseType="Collection">
			<editHistoryEntry>
				<changeDescription>Created definition to match the class definition it references.</changeDescription>
				<changeVersion>14.0.0.0</changeVersion>
				<issueLink>https://github.com/CEDStandards/CEDS-Ontology/issues/110</issueLink>
				<changeUpdated rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#boolean">true</changeUpdated>
			</editHistoryEntry>
		</editHistory>
	</rdf:Property>
	<rdf:Property rdf:about="https://w3id.org/CEDStandards/terms/P001525">
		<dc:creator>Common Education Data Standards</dc:creator>
		<dc:identifier rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#token">P001525</dc:identifier>
		<rdfs:label>Has Competency Definition Current Version Indicator</rdfs:label>
		<schema:domainIncludes rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/CEDStandards/terms/C200065" />
		<schema:rangeIncludes rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/CEDStandards/terms/C001525" />
		<skos:notation>hasCompetencyDefinitionCurrentVersionIndicator</skos:notation>
		<dc:description>Indicates that this is the most current version of the Competency Definition.</dc:description>
		<rdfs:comment>This element supports version histories at the statement level. If corrections have been made to individual items/statements that are not part of a new Competency Framework, the elements 'Competency Definition Previous Version Identifier' and 'Competency Definition Current Version Indicator' provide a reference to historical versions of the current statement. In such uses the 'Competency Definition Code' could be the same for multiple versions of a statement and 'Competency Definition URL' could resolve to the most current version of the statement.</rdfs:comment>
		<editHistory rdf:parseType="Collection"> 
			<editHistoryEntry> 	
				<changeDescription>Entity name changed from "Competency Item" to "Competency Definition" to support alignment across standards and reduce confusion by those who might think this is a "competency assertion" that is attributed to a person rather than what it is, a definition of a competency that could apply to any person.</changeDescription> 	
				<changeVersion>8</changeVersion> 
			</editHistoryEntry>
		</editHistory>
		<skos:definition>Indicates that this is the most current version of the Competency Definition.</skos:definition>
	</rdf:Property>
	<rdf:Property rdf:about="https://w3id.org/CEDStandards/terms/P600303">
		<dc:creator>Common Education Data Standards</dc:creator>
		<dc:identifier rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#token">P600303</dc:identifier>
		<rdfs:label>Has Competency Framework</rdfs:label>
		<schema:domainIncludes rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/CEDStandards/terms/C200065" />
		<schema:rangeIncludes rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/CEDStandards/terms/C200067" />
		<skos:notation>hasCompetencyFramework</skos:notation>
		<dc:description>References a resource that identifies a collection of logically related CompetencyDefinitions, CompetencyDefAssociations, and contextualizing metadata.</dc:description>
		<skos:definition>References a resource that identifies a collection of logically related CompetencyDefinitions, CompetencyDefAssociations, and contextualizing metadata.</skos:definition>
		<editHistory rdf:parseType="Collection">
			<editHistoryEntry>
				<changeDescription>Created definition to match the class definition it references.</changeDescription>
				<changeVersion>14.0.0.0</changeVersion>
				<issueLink>https://github.com/CEDStandards/CEDS-Ontology/issues/110</issueLink>
				<changeUpdated rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#boolean">true</changeUpdated>
			</editHistoryEntry>
		</editHistory>
	</rdf:Property>
	<rdf:Property rdf:about="https://w3id.org/CEDStandards/terms/P600348">
		<dc:creator>Common Education Data Standards</dc:creator>
		<dc:identifier rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#token">P600348</dc:identifier>
		<rdfs:label>Has Competency Set</rdfs:label>
		<schema:domainIncludes rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/CEDStandards/terms/C200065" />
		<schema:domainIncludes rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/CEDStandards/terms/C200146" />
		<schema:domainIncludes rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/CEDStandards/terms/C200312" />
		<schema:rangeIncludes rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/CEDStandards/terms/C200068" />
		<skos:notation>hasCompetencySet</skos:notation>
		<dc:description>References competencySet supports defining criteria for award or recognition of a credential or micro-credential based on a person's attainment of one or more CompetencyFrameworkItem(s). The set may have a completion criteria specifying if all or some of the items are required. If only some are required then Completion Criteria Threshold is used to specify how many. Competency Set may also include other Competency Sets so it is possible to make a rule such as "the person must complete these three required competency items and 2 out of 3 of these items specified in this sub set."</dc:description>
		<skos:definition>References competencySet supports defining criteria for award or recognition of a credential or micro-credential based on a person's attainment of one or more CompetencyFrameworkItem(s). The set may have a completion criteria specifying if all or some of the items are required. If only some are required then Completion Criteria Threshold is used to specify how many. Competency Set may also include other Competency Sets so it is possible to make a rule such as "the person must complete these three required competency items and 2 out of 3 of these items specified in this sub set."</skos:definition>
		<editHistory rdf:parseType="Collection">
			<editHistoryEntry>
				<changeDescription>Created definition to match the class definition it references.</changeDescription>
				<changeVersion>14.0.0.0</changeVersion>
				<issueLink>https://github.com/CEDStandards/CEDS-Ontology/issues/110</issueLink>
				<changeUpdated rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#boolean">true</changeUpdated>
			</editHistoryEntry>
		</editHistory>
	</rdf:Property>
	<rdf:Property rdf:about="https://w3id.org/CEDStandards/terms/P000875">
		<dc:creator>Common Education Data Standards</dc:creator>
		<dc:identifier rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#token">P000875</dc:identifier>
		<rdfs:label>Has Competency Definition Blooms Taxonomy Domain</rdfs:label>
		<schema:domainIncludes rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/CEDStandards/terms/C200065" />
		<schema:rangeIncludes rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/CEDStandards/terms/C000875" />
		<skos:notation>hasCompetencyDefinitionBloomsTaxonomyDomain</skos:notation>
		<dc:description>Classification of the Competency Definition using Bloom's Taxonomy Domains.</dc:description>
		<editHistory rdf:parseType="Collection"> 
			<editHistoryEntry> 	
				<changeDescription>Entity name changed from "Competency Item" to "Competency Definition" to support alignment across standards and reduce confusion by those who might think this is a "competency assertion" that is attributed to a person rather than what it is, a definition of a competency that could apply to any person.</changeDescription> 	
				<changeVersion>8</changeVersion> 
			</editHistoryEntry>
		</editHistory>
		<skos:definition>Classification of the Competency Definition using Bloom's Taxonomy Domains.</skos:definition>
	</rdf:Property>
	<rdf:Property rdf:about="https://w3id.org/CEDStandards/terms/P000881">
		<dc:creator>Common Education Data Standards</dc:creator>
		<dc:identifier rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#token">P000881</dc:identifier>
		<rdfs:label>Has Competency Definition Language</rdfs:label>
		<schema:domainIncludes rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/CEDStandards/terms/C200065" />
		<schema:rangeIncludes rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/CEDStandards/terms/C000317" />
		<skos:notation>hasCompetencyDefinitionLanguage</skos:notation>
		<dc:description>The default language of the text used for the content in the competency definition statement.</dc:description>
		<rdfs:comment>The CEDS ISO 639-2 Language Code option set comes from the &lt;a href="http://www.loc.gov/standards/iso639-2/langhome.html"&gt;ISO 639-2 standard&lt;/a&gt;, the character encoding in ISO 8859-1 download.  Discontinued codes from the ISO standard are not included in the CEDS list.</rdfs:comment>
		<skos:definition>The default language of the text used for the content in the competency definition statement.</skos:definition>
		<editHistory rdf:parseType="Collection"> 
			<editHistoryEntry> 	
				<changeDescription>Entity name changed from "Competency Item" to "Competency Definition" to support alignment across standards and reduce confusion by those who might think this is a "competency assertion" that is attributed to a person rather than what it is, a definition of a competency that could apply to any person. Updating to reflect the latest version of the ISO 639-2 standard.</changeDescription> 	
				<changeVersion>8</changeVersion> 
			</editHistoryEntry> 
			<editHistoryEntry> 	
				<changeDescription>Updated to reflect the latest version of the ISO 639-2 standard.</changeDescription> 	
				<changeVersion>9</changeVersion> 
			</editHistoryEntry>
		</editHistory>
	</rdf:Property>
	<rdf:Property rdf:about="https://w3id.org/CEDStandards/terms/P000876">
		<dc:creator>Common Education Data Standards</dc:creator>
		<dc:identifier rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#token">P000876</dc:identifier>
		<rdfs:label>Has Competency Definition Multiple Intelligence</rdfs:label>
		<schema:domainIncludes rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/CEDStandards/terms/C200065" />
		<schema:rangeIncludes rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/CEDStandards/terms/C000876" />
		<skos:notation>hasCompetencyDefinitionMultipleIntelligence</skos:notation>
		<dc:description>Classification of the Competency Definition using intelligences defined for Howard Earl Gardner's Theory of Multiple Intelligences.</dc:description>
		<editHistory rdf:parseType="Collection"> 
			<editHistoryEntry> 	
				<changeDescription>Entity name changed from "Competency Item" to "Competency Definition" to support alignment across standards and reduce confusion by those who might think this is a "competency assertion" that is attributed to a person rather than what it is, a definition of a competency that could apply to any person.</changeDescription> 	
				<changeVersion>8</changeVersion> 
			</editHistoryEntry>
		</editHistory>
		<skos:definition>Classification of the Competency Definition using intelligences defined for Howard Earl Gardner's Theory of Multiple Intelligences.</skos:definition>
	</rdf:Property>
	<rdf:Property rdf:about="https://w3id.org/CEDStandards/terms/P001408">
		<dc:creator>Common Education Data Standards</dc:creator>
		<dc:identifier rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#token">P001408</dc:identifier>
		<rdfs:label>Has Competency Definition Node Accessibility Profile</rdfs:label>
		<schema:domainIncludes rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/CEDStandards/terms/C200065" />
		<schema:rangeIncludes rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/CEDStandards/terms/C001408" />
		<skos:notation>hasCompetencyDefinitionNodeAccessibilityProfile</skos:notation>
		<dc:description>When the Competency Definition is used as a node in a learning map, this element supports alternative pathways based on a learner's accessibility profile. The type selected indicates which accessibility profile the node is designed to address.</dc:description>
		<editHistory rdf:parseType="Collection"> 
			<editHistoryEntry> 	
				<changeDescription>Entity name changed from "Competency Item" to "Competency Definition" to support alignment across standards and reduce confusion by those who might think this is a "competency assertion" that is attributed to a person rather than what it is, a definition of a competency that could apply to any person.</changeDescription> 	
				<changeVersion>8</changeVersion> 
			</editHistoryEntry>
		</editHistory>
		<skos:definition>When the Competency Definition is used as a node in a learning map, this element supports alternative pathways based on a learner's accessibility profile. The type selected indicates which accessibility profile the node is designed to address.</skos:definition>
	</rdf:Property>
	<rdf:Property rdf:about="https://w3id.org/CEDStandards/terms/P001411">
		<dc:creator>Common Education Data Standards</dc:creator>
		<dc:identifier rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#token">P001411</dc:identifier>
		<rdfs:label>Has Competency Definition Testability Type</rdfs:label>
		<schema:domainIncludes rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/CEDStandards/terms/C200065" />
		<schema:rangeIncludes rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/CEDStandards/terms/C001411" />
		<skos:notation>hasCompetencyDefinitionTestabilityType</skos:notation>
		<dc:description>Indicates if the competency described in the Competency Definition Statement can be tested using one or more assessment items.</dc:description>
		<editHistory rdf:parseType="Collection"> 
			<editHistoryEntry> 	
				<changeDescription>Entity name changed from "Competency Item" to "Competency Definition" to support alignment across standards and reduce confusion by those who might think this is a "competency assertion" that is attributed to a person rather than what it is, a definition of a competency that could apply to any person.</changeDescription> 	
				<changeVersion>8</changeVersion> 
			</editHistoryEntry>
		</editHistory>
		<skos:definition>Indicates if the competency described in the Competency Definition Statement can be tested using one or more assessment items.</skos:definition>
	</rdf:Property>
	<rdf:Property rdf:about="https://w3id.org/CEDStandards/terms/P000880">
		<dc:creator>Common Education Data Standards</dc:creator>
		<dc:identifier rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#token">P000880</dc:identifier>
