	<owl:Class rdf:about="https://w3id.org/CEDStandards/terms/C000862">
		<dc:creator>Common Education Data Standards</dc:creator>
		<dc:description>Rural-Urban Continuum Codes form a classification scheme that distinguishes metropolitan (metro) counties by the population size of their metro area, and nonmetropolitan (nonmetro) counties by degree of urbanization and adjacency to a metro area or areas. The metro and nonmetro categories have been subdivided into three metro and six nonmetro groupings, resulting in a nine-part county codification. The codes allow researchers working with county data to break such data into finer residential groups beyond a simple metro-nonmetro dichotomy, particularly for the analysis of trends in nonmetro areas that may be related to degree of rurality and metro proximity.</dc:description>
		<dc:identifier rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#token">C000862</dc:identifier>
		<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#ConceptScheme" />
		<rdfs:label>Economic Research Service Rural-Urban Continuum Code</rdfs:label>
		<rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/CEDStandards/terms/C000000" />
		<skos:definition>Rural-Urban Continuum Codes form a classification scheme that distinguishes metropolitan (metro) counties by the population size of their metro area, and nonmetropolitan (nonmetro) counties by degree of urbanization and adjacency to a metro area or areas. The metro and nonmetro categories have been subdivided into three metro and six nonmetro groupings, resulting in a nine-part county codification. The codes allow researchers working with county data to break such data into finer residential groups beyond a simple metro-nonmetro dichotomy, particularly for the analysis of trends in nonmetro areas that may be related to degree of rurality and metro proximity.</skos:definition>
		<skos:notation>ERSRuralUrbanContinuumCode</skos:notation>
		<skos:prefLabel>Economic Research Service Rural-Urban Continuum Code</skos:prefLabel>
	</owl:Class>
	<owl:Class rdf:about="https://w3id.org/CEDStandards/terms/C000867">
