	<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="https://w3id.org/CEDStandards/terms/NI001517162997">
		<dc:creator>Common Education Data Standards</dc:creator>
		<dc:description>Korean for Young Learners (prior-to-secondary) courses provide instruction at multiple grade levels in Korean and may apply to a range of consecutive grades. These courses prepare students to communicate authentically in Korean by interpreting (reading, listening, viewing), exchanging (speaking and listening; reading and writing), and presenting (speaking, writing) information on concrete topics. These courses introduce the relationships among the products, practices, and perspectives of Korean-speaking cultures.</dc:description>
		<dc:identifier rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#token">NI001517162997</dc:identifier>
		<rdf:type rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/CEDStandards/terms/C001517" />
		<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept" />
		<rdfs:label>Korean for Young Learners (prior-to-secondary)</rdfs:label>
		<skos:definition>Korean for Young Learners (prior-to-secondary) courses provide instruction at multiple grade levels in Korean and may apply to a range of consecutive grades. These courses prepare students to communicate authentically in Korean by interpreting (reading, listening, viewing), exchanging (speaking and listening; reading and writing), and presenting (speaking, writing) information on concrete topics. These courses introduce the relationships among the products, practices, and perspectives of Korean-speaking cultures.</skos:definition>
		<skos:inScheme rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/CEDStandards/terms/C001517" />
		<skos:notation>24500</skos:notation>
		<skos:prefLabel>Korean for Young Learners (prior-to-secondary)</skos:prefLabel>
	</owl:NamedIndividual>
	<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="https://w3id.org/CEDStandards/terms/NI001517163003">
		<dc:creator>Common Education Data Standards</dc:creator>
		<dc:description>Early Childhood Education courses involve content that is not differentiated by subject area. These courses focus on content that is grade-specific and cover various subjects throughout the day, rather than a single subject-specific content area. Specific course content depends upon state standards for early childhood education.</dc:description>
		<dc:identifier rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#token">NI001517163003</dc:identifier>
		<rdf:type rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/CEDStandards/terms/C001517" />
		<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept" />
		<rdfs:label>Early Childhood Education</rdfs:label>
		<skos:definition>Early Childhood Education courses involve content that is not differentiated by subject area. These courses focus on content that is grade-specific and cover various subjects throughout the day, rather than a single subject-specific content area. Specific course content depends upon state standards for early childhood education.</skos:definition>
		<skos:inScheme rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/CEDStandards/terms/C001517" />
		<skos:notation>23001</skos:notation>
		<skos:prefLabel>Early Childhood Education</skos:prefLabel>
	</owl:NamedIndividual>
	<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="https://w3id.org/CEDStandards/terms/NI001517162998">
		<dc:creator>Common Education Data Standards</dc:creator>
		<dc:description>Korean Immersion (prior-to-secondary) courses engage students in developmentally appropriate activities to acquire literacy in Korean and grade-specific content using Korean as the language of instruction. Korean Immersion courses prepare students to communicate authentically in Korean by interpreting (reading, listening, viewing), exchanging (speaking and listening; reading and writing), and presenting (speaking, writing) information about standards-based academic content and incorporate the relationships among the products, practices, and perspectives of Korean-speaking cultures.</dc:description>
		<dc:identifier rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#token">NI001517162998</dc:identifier>
		<rdf:type rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/CEDStandards/terms/C001517" />
		<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept" />
		<rdfs:label>Korean Immersion (prior-to-secondary)</rdfs:label>
		<skos:definition>Korean Immersion (prior-to-secondary) courses engage students in developmentally appropriate activities to acquire literacy in Korean and grade-specific content using Korean as the language of instruction. Korean Immersion courses prepare students to communicate authentically in Korean by interpreting (reading, listening, viewing), exchanging (speaking and listening; reading and writing), and presenting (speaking, writing) information about standards-based academic content and incorporate the relationships among the products, practices, and perspectives of Korean-speaking cultures.</skos:definition>
		<skos:inScheme rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/CEDStandards/terms/C001517" />
		<skos:notation>24501</skos:notation>
		<skos:prefLabel>Korean Immersion (prior-to-secondary)</skos:prefLabel>
	</owl:NamedIndividual>
	<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="https://w3id.org/CEDStandards/terms/NI001517162999">
		<dc:creator>Common Education Data Standards</dc:creator>
		<dc:description>Designed to introduce students to Korean language and culture, Korean I courses prepare students to communicate authentically in Korean by interpreting (reading, listening, viewing), exchanging (speaking and listening; reading and writing), and presenting (speaking, writing) information on a variety of topics. They introduce the relationships among the products, practices, and perspectives of Korean-speaking cultures.</dc:description>
		<dc:identifier rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#token">NI001517162999</dc:identifier>
		<rdf:type rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/CEDStandards/terms/C001517" />
		<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept" />
		<rdfs:label>Korean I</rdfs:label>
		<skos:definition>Designed to introduce students to Korean language and culture, Korean I courses prepare students to communicate authentically in Korean by interpreting (reading, listening, viewing), exchanging (speaking and listening; reading and writing), and presenting (speaking, writing) information on a variety of topics. They introduce the relationships among the products, practices, and perspectives of Korean-speaking cultures.</skos:definition>
		<skos:inScheme rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/CEDStandards/terms/C001517" />
		<skos:notation>24502</skos:notation>
		<skos:prefLabel>Korean I</skos:prefLabel>
	</owl:NamedIndividual>
	<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="https://w3id.org/CEDStandards/terms/NI001517163000">
		<dc:creator>Common Education Data Standards</dc:creator>
		<dc:description>Korean II courses build upon skills developed in Korean I, preparing students to communicate authentically in Korean by interpreting (reading, listening, viewing), exchanging (speaking and listening; reading and writing), and presenting (speaking, writing) information on concrete topics. Korean II courses introduce the relationships among the products, practices, and perspectives of Korean-speaking cultures.</dc:description>
		<dc:identifier rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#token">NI001517163000</dc:identifier>
		<rdf:type rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/CEDStandards/terms/C001517" />
		<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept" />
		<rdfs:label>Korean II</rdfs:label>
		<skos:definition>Korean II courses build upon skills developed in Korean I, preparing students to communicate authentically in Korean by interpreting (reading, listening, viewing), exchanging (speaking and listening; reading and writing), and presenting (speaking, writing) information on concrete topics. Korean II courses introduce the relationships among the products, practices, and perspectives of Korean-speaking cultures.</skos:definition>
		<skos:inScheme rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/CEDStandards/terms/C001517" />
		<skos:notation>24503</skos:notation>
		<skos:prefLabel>Korean II</skos:prefLabel>
	</owl:NamedIndividual>
	<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="https://w3id.org/CEDStandards/terms/NI001517163001">
		<dc:creator>Common Education Data Standards</dc:creator>
		<dc:description>Korean III courses prepare students to communicate authentically in Korean by interpreting (reading, listening, viewing), exchanging (speaking and listening; reading and writing), and presenting (speaking, writing) information, concepts, and ideas on a variety of topics, including connections to other subject areas. These courses expand students' knowledge of relationships among the products, practices, and perspectives of Korean-speaking countries and cultures.</dc:description>
		<dc:identifier rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#token">NI001517163001</dc:identifier>
		<rdf:type rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/CEDStandards/terms/C001517" />
		<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept" />
		<rdfs:label>Korean III</rdfs:label>
		<skos:definition>Korean III courses prepare students to communicate authentically in Korean by interpreting (reading, listening, viewing), exchanging (speaking and listening; reading and writing), and presenting (speaking, writing) information, concepts, and ideas on a variety of topics, including connections to other subject areas. These courses expand students' knowledge of relationships among the products, practices, and perspectives of Korean-speaking countries and cultures.</skos:definition>
		<skos:inScheme rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/CEDStandards/terms/C001517"/>
		<skos:notation>24504</skos:notation>
		<skos:prefLabel>Korean III</skos:prefLabel>
	</owl:NamedIndividual>
	<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="https://w3id.org/CEDStandards/terms/NI001517163002">
		<dc:creator>Common Education Data Standards</dc:creator>
		<dc:description>Pre-kindergarten courses involve content that is not differentiated by subject area. These courses focus on content that is grade-specific and cover various subjects throughout the day, rather than a single subject-specific content area. Specific course content depends upon state standards for pre-kindergarten.</dc:description>
		<dc:identifier rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#token">NI001517163002</dc:identifier>
