		<skos:definition>IB Language A: Language and Literature�English courses prepare students to take the International Baccalaureate Language A: Language and Literature exams. Course content includes in-depth study of various text types and literary forms, composition for purpose and audience, and the context and elements of literature. The course includes oral and written assignments and is designed for students highly competent in using English in an academic context.</skos:definition>
		<skos:inScheme rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/CEDStandards/terms/C001517" />
