		<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept" />
		<rdfs:label>Cash With Fiscal Agents</rdfs:label>
		<skos:definition>Deposits with fiscal agents, such as commercial banks, for paying matured bonds and interest.</skos:definition>
		<skos:inScheme rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/CEDStandards/terms/C001353" />
		<skos:notation>105</skos:notation>
		<skos:prefLabel>Cash With Fiscal Agents</skos:prefLabel>
	</owl:NamedIndividual>
	<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="https://w3id.org/CEDStandards/terms/NI001353117337">
		<dc:creator>Common Education Data Standards</dc:creator>
		<dc:description>Securities and real estate held for producing income in the form of interest, dividends, rentals, or lease payments. Investments should be presented at fair value as of the reporting date. Gains from changes in the fair value of investments are recorded using revenue account 1530. Losses from changes in the fair value of investments are recorded using expenditure object code 930. Alternatively, gains and losses may be netted and recorded in revenue account 1530. The account does not include capital assets used in school district operations. Separate accounts may be maintained for each category of investments.</dc:description>
		<dc:identifier rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#token">NI001353117337</dc:identifier>
		<rdf:type rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/CEDStandards/terms/C001353" />
		<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept" />
		<rdfs:label>Investments</rdfs:label>
		<skos:definition>Securities and real estate held for producing income in the form of interest, dividends, rentals, or lease payments. Investments should be presented at fair value as of the reporting date. Gains from changes in the fair value of investments are recorded using revenue account 1530. Losses from changes in the fair value of investments are recorded using expenditure object code 930. Alternatively, gains and losses may be netted and recorded in revenue account 1530. The account does not include capital assets used in school district operations. Separate accounts may be maintained for each category of investments.</skos:definition>
		<skos:inScheme rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/CEDStandards/terms/C001353" />
		<skos:notation>111</skos:notation>
		<skos:prefLabel>Investments</skos:prefLabel>
	</owl:NamedIndividual>
	<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="https://w3id.org/CEDStandards/terms/NI001353117338">
		<dc:creator>Common Education Data Standards</dc:creator>
		<dc:description>The excess of the amount paid for securities over the face value that has not yet been amortized. Use of this account is restricted to short- term money market investments.</dc:description>
		<dc:identifier rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#token">NI001353117338</dc:identifier>
		<rdf:type rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/CEDStandards/terms/C001353" />
		<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept" />
		<rdfs:label>Unamortized Premiums on Investments</rdfs:label>
		<skos:definition>The excess of the amount paid for securities over the face value that has not yet been amortized. Use of this account is restricted to short- term money market investments.</skos:definition>
		<skos:inScheme rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/CEDStandards/terms/C001353" />
		<skos:notation>112</skos:notation>
		<skos:prefLabel>Unamortized Premiums on Investments</skos:prefLabel>
	</owl:NamedIndividual>
	<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="https://w3id.org/CEDStandards/terms/NI001353117339">
		<dc:creator>Common Education Data Standards</dc:creator>
		<dc:description>The excess of the face value of securities over the amount paid for them that has not yet been written off. Use of this account is restricted to short-term investments.</dc:description>
		<dc:identifier rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#token">NI001353117339</dc:identifier>
		<rdf:type rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/CEDStandards/terms/C001353" />
		<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept" />
		<rdfs:label>Unamortized Discounts on Investments (Credit)</rdfs:label>
		<skos:definition>The excess of the face value of securities over the amount paid for them that has not yet been written off. Use of this account is restricted to short-term investments.</skos:definition>
		<skos:inScheme rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/CEDStandards/terms/C001353" />
		<skos:notation>113</skos:notation>
		<skos:prefLabel>Unamortized Discounts on Investments (Credit)</skos:prefLabel>
	</owl:NamedIndividual>
	<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="https://w3id.org/CEDStandards/terms/NI001353117340">
		<dc:creator>Common Education Data Standards</dc:creator>
		<dc:description>The amount of interest receivable on investments, excluding interest purchased. Interest purchased should be shown in a separate account.</dc:description>
		<dc:identifier rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#token">NI001353117340</dc:identifier>
		<rdf:type rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/CEDStandards/terms/C001353" />
		<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept" />
		<rdfs:label>Interest Receivable on Investments</rdfs:label>
		<skos:definition>The amount of interest receivable on investments, excluding interest purchased. Interest purchased should be shown in a separate account.</skos:definition>
		<skos:inScheme rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/CEDStandards/terms/C001353" />
		<skos:notation>114</skos:notation>
		<skos:prefLabel>Interest Receivable on Investments</skos:prefLabel>
	</owl:NamedIndividual>
	<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="https://w3id.org/CEDStandards/terms/NI001353117341">
		<dc:creator>Common Education Data Standards</dc:creator>
		<dc:description>Interest accrued on investments between the last interest payment date and the date of purchase. The account is carried as an asset until the first interest payment date after the date of purchase.</dc:description>
		<dc:identifier rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#token">NI001353117341</dc:identifier>
		<rdf:type rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/CEDStandards/terms/C001353" />
		<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept" />
		<rdfs:label>Accrued Interest on Investments Purchased</rdfs:label>
		<skos:definition>Interest accrued on investments between the last interest payment date and the date of purchase. The account is carried as an asset until the first interest payment date after the date of purchase.</skos:definition>
		<skos:inScheme rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/CEDStandards/terms/C001353" />
		<skos:notation>115</skos:notation>
		<skos:prefLabel>Accrued Interest on Investments Purchased</skos:prefLabel>
	</owl:NamedIndividual>
	<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="https://w3id.org/CEDStandards/terms/NI001353117342">
		<dc:creator>Common Education Data Standards</dc:creator>
		<dc:description>The uncollected portion of taxes that a school district or government unit has levied and that has become due, including any interest or penalties that may be accrued. Separate accounts may be maintained on the basis of tax roll year, current and delinquent taxes, or both.</dc:description>
		<dc:identifier rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#token">NI001353117342</dc:identifier>
		<rdf:type rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/CEDStandards/terms/C001353" />
		<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept" />
		<rdfs:label>Taxes Receivable</rdfs:label>
		<skos:definition>The uncollected portion of taxes that a school district or government unit has levied and that has become due, including any interest or penalties that may be accrued. Separate accounts may be maintained on the basis of tax roll year, current and delinquent taxes, or both.</skos:definition>
		<skos:inScheme rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/CEDStandards/terms/C001353" />
		<skos:notation>121</skos:notation>
		<skos:prefLabel>Taxes Receivable</skos:prefLabel>
	</owl:NamedIndividual>
	<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="https://w3id.org/CEDStandards/terms/NI001353117343">
		<dc:creator>Common Education Data Standards</dc:creator>
		<dc:description>The portion of taxes receivable estimated not to be collected. The account is shown on the balance sheet as a deduction from the taxes receivable account to arrive at the net taxes receivable. Separate accounts may be maintained on the basis of tax roll year, delinquent taxes, or both.</dc:description>
		<dc:identifier rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#token">NI001353117343</dc:identifier>
		<rdf:type rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/CEDStandards/terms/C001353" />
		<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept" />
		<rdfs:label>Allowance for Uncollectible Taxes (Credit)</rdfs:label>
		<skos:definition>The portion of taxes receivable estimated not to be collected. The account is shown on the balance sheet as a deduction from the taxes receivable account to arrive at the net taxes receivable. Separate accounts may be maintained on the basis of tax roll year, delinquent taxes, or both.</skos:definition>
		<skos:inScheme rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/CEDStandards/terms/C001353" />
		<skos:notation>122</skos:notation>
		<skos:prefLabel>Allowance for Uncollectible Taxes (Credit)</skos:prefLabel>
	</owl:NamedIndividual>
	<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="https://w3id.org/CEDStandards/terms/NI001353117344">
		<dc:creator>Common Education Data Standards</dc:creator>
		<dc:description>An asset account used to record a loan by one fund to another fund in the same governmental unit. It is recommended that separate accounts be maintained for each interfund receivable loan.</dc:description>
		<dc:identifier rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#token">NI001353117344</dc:identifier>
		<rdf:type rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/CEDStandards/terms/C001353" />
		<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept" />
		<rdfs:label>Interfund Loans Receivable</rdfs:label>
		<skos:definition>An asset account used to record a loan by one fund to another fund in the same governmental unit. It is recommended that separate accounts be maintained for each interfund receivable loan.</skos:definition>
		<skos:inScheme rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/CEDStandards/terms/C001353" />
		<skos:notation>131</skos:notation>
		<skos:prefLabel>Interfund Loans Receivable</skos:prefLabel>
	</owl:NamedIndividual>
	<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="https://w3id.org/CEDStandards/terms/NI001353117345">
		<dc:creator>Common Education Data Standards</dc:creator>
		<dc:description>An asset account used to indicate amounts owed to a particular fund by another fund in the same school district for goods sold or services rendered. It is recommended that separate accounts be maintained for each interfund receivable.</dc:description>
		<dc:identifier rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#token">NI001353117345</dc:identifier>
		<rdf:type rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/CEDStandards/terms/C001353" />
		<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept" />
		<rdfs:label>Interfund Accounts Receivable</rdfs:label>
		<skos:definition>An asset account used to indicate amounts owed to a particular fund by another fund in the same school district for goods sold or services rendered. It is recommended that separate accounts be maintained for each interfund receivable.</skos:definition>
		<skos:inScheme rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/CEDStandards/terms/C001353" />
		<skos:notation>132</skos:notation>
		<skos:prefLabel>Interfund Accounts Receivable</skos:prefLabel>
	</owl:NamedIndividual>
	<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="https://w3id.org/CEDStandards/terms/NI001353117346">
		<dc:creator>Common Education Data Standards</dc:creator>
		<dc:description>Amounts due to the reporting governmental unit from another governmental unit. These amounts may represent grants-in-aid, shared taxes, taxes collected for the reporting unit by another unit, loans, and charges for services rendered by the reporting unit for another government. It is recommended that separate accounts be maintained for each interagency receivable.</dc:description>
		<dc:identifier rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#token">NI001353117346</dc:identifier>
		<rdf:type rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/CEDStandards/terms/C001353" />
		<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept" />
		<rdfs:label>Intergovernmental Accounts Receivable</rdfs:label>
		<skos:definition>Amounts due to the reporting governmental unit from another governmental unit. These amounts may represent grants-in-aid, shared taxes, taxes collected for the reporting unit by another unit, loans, and charges for services rendered by the reporting unit for another government. It is recommended that separate accounts be maintained for each interagency receivable.</skos:definition>
		<skos:inScheme rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/CEDStandards/terms/C001353" />
		<skos:notation>141</skos:notation>
		<skos:prefLabel>Intergovernmental Accounts Receivable</skos:prefLabel>
	</owl:NamedIndividual>
	<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="https://w3id.org/CEDStandards/terms/NI001353117347">
		<dc:creator>Common Education Data Standards</dc:creator>
		<dc:description>Amounts that have been loaned to persons or organizations, including notes taken as security for such loans, where permitted by statutory authority.</dc:description>
		<dc:identifier rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#token">NI001353117347</dc:identifier>
		<rdf:type rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/CEDStandards/terms/C001353" />
		<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept" />
		<rdfs:label>Loans Receivable</rdfs:label>
		<skos:definition>Amounts that have been loaned to persons or organizations, including notes taken as security for such loans, where permitted by statutory authority.</skos:definition>
		<skos:inScheme rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/CEDStandards/terms/C001353" />
		<skos:notation>151</skos:notation>
		<skos:prefLabel>Loans Receivable</skos:prefLabel>
	</owl:NamedIndividual>
	<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="https://w3id.org/CEDStandards/terms/NI001353117348">
		<dc:creator>Common Education Data Standards</dc:creator>
		<dc:description>The portion of loans receivable estimated not to be collected. The account is shown on the balance sheet as a deduction from the other loans receivable account.</dc:description>
		<dc:identifier rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#token">NI001353117348</dc:identifier>
		<rdf:type rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/CEDStandards/terms/C001353" />
		<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept" />
		<rdfs:label>Allowance for Uncollectible Loans (Credit)</rdfs:label>
		<skos:definition>The portion of loans receivable estimated not to be collected. The account is shown on the balance sheet as a deduction from the other loans receivable account.</skos:definition>
		<skos:inScheme rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/CEDStandards/terms/C001353" />
		<skos:notation>152</skos:notation>
		<skos:prefLabel>Allowance for Uncollectible Loans (Credit)</skos:prefLabel>
	</owl:NamedIndividual>
	<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="https://w3id.org/CEDStandards/terms/NI001353117349">
		<dc:creator>Common Education Data Standards</dc:creator>
		<dc:description>Amounts due on open account from private persons, firms, or corporations for goods and services furnished by a school district (but not including amounts due from other funds or from other governmental units).</dc:description>
		<dc:identifier rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#token">NI001353117349</dc:identifier>
		<rdf:type rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/CEDStandards/terms/C001353" />
		<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept" />
		<rdfs:label>Other Accounts Receivable</rdfs:label>
		<skos:definition>Amounts due on open account from private persons, firms, or corporations for goods and services furnished by a school district (but not including amounts due from other funds or from other governmental units).</skos:definition>
		<skos:inScheme rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/CEDStandards/terms/C001353" />
		<skos:notation>153</skos:notation>
		<skos:prefLabel>Other Accounts Receivable</skos:prefLabel>
	</owl:NamedIndividual>
	<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="https://w3id.org/CEDStandards/terms/NI001353117350">
		<dc:creator>Common Education Data Standards</dc:creator>
		<dc:description>A provision for that portion of accounts receivable that is estimated will not be collected. The account is shown on the balance sheet as a deduction from the other accounts receivable account.</dc:description>
		<dc:identifier rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#token">NI001353117350</dc:identifier>
		<rdf:type rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/CEDStandards/terms/C001353" />
		<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept" />
		<rdfs:label>Allowance for Uncollectible Accounts Receivable (Credit)</rdfs:label>
		<skos:definition>A provision for that portion of accounts receivable that is estimated will not be collected. The account is shown on the balance sheet as a deduction from the other accounts receivable account.</skos:definition>
		<skos:inScheme rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/CEDStandards/terms/C001353" />
		<skos:notation>154</skos:notation>
		<skos:prefLabel>Allowance for Uncollectible Accounts Receivable (Credit)</skos:prefLabel>
	</owl:NamedIndividual>
	<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="https://w3id.org/CEDStandards/terms/NI001353117351">
		<dc:creator>Common Education Data Standards</dc:creator>
		<dc:description>The cost of supplies and equipment on hand not yet distributed to requisitioning units.</dc:description>
		<dc:identifier rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#token">NI001353117351</dc:identifier>
		<rdf:type rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/CEDStandards/terms/C001353" />
		<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept" />
		<rdfs:label>Inventories for Consumption</rdfs:label>
		<skos:definition>The cost of supplies and equipment on hand not yet distributed to requisitioning units.</skos:definition>
		<skos:inScheme rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/CEDStandards/terms/C001353" />
		<skos:notation>171</skos:notation>
		<skos:prefLabel>Inventories for Consumption</skos:prefLabel>
	</owl:NamedIndividual>
	<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="https://w3id.org/CEDStandards/terms/NI001353117352">
		<dc:creator>Common Education Data Standards</dc:creator>
		<dc:description>The value of goods purchased and held by a school district for resale rather than for use in its own operations. Such goods could include unique manufactured inventories, such as student-built homes or equipment.</dc:description>
		<dc:identifier rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#token">NI001353117352</dc:identifier>
		<rdf:type rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/CEDStandards/terms/C001353" />
		<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept" />
		<rdfs:label>Inventories for Resale</rdfs:label>
		<skos:definition>The value of goods purchased and held by a school district for resale rather than for use in its own operations. Such goods could include unique manufactured inventories, such as student-built homes or equipment.</skos:definition>
		<skos:inScheme rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/CEDStandards/terms/C001353" />
		<skos:notation>172</skos:notation>
		<skos:prefLabel>Inventories for Resale</skos:prefLabel>
	</owl:NamedIndividual>
	<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="https://w3id.org/CEDStandards/terms/NI001353117353">
		<dc:creator>Common Education Data Standards</dc:creator>
		<dc:description>Expenditures/expenses paid for benefits not yet received. Prepaid expenses differ from deferred charges in that they are spread over a shorter period of time and are regularly recurring costs of operation. Examples of prepaid expenses are prepaid rent, prepaid interest, and unexpired insurance premiums.</dc:description>
		<dc:identifier rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#token">NI001353117353</dc:identifier>
		<rdf:type rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/CEDStandards/terms/C001353" />
		<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept" />
		<rdfs:label>Prepaid Items</rdfs:label>
		<skos:definition>Expenditures/expenses paid for benefits not yet received. Prepaid expenses differ from deferred charges in that they are spread over a shorter period of time and are regularly recurring costs of operation. Examples of prepaid expenses are prepaid rent, prepaid interest, and unexpired insurance premiums.</skos:definition>
		<skos:inScheme rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/CEDStandards/terms/C001353" />
		<skos:notation>181</skos:notation>
		<skos:prefLabel>Prepaid Items</skos:prefLabel>
	</owl:NamedIndividual>
	<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="https://w3id.org/CEDStandards/terms/NI001353117354">
		<dc:creator>Common Education Data Standards</dc:creator>
		<dc:description>Funds deposited by the school district as a prerequisite to receiving services, goods, or both.</dc:description>
		<dc:identifier rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#token">NI001353117354</dc:identifier>
		<rdf:type rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/CEDStandards/terms/C001353" />
		<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept" />
		<rdfs:label>Deposits</rdfs:label>
		<skos:definition>Funds deposited by the school district as a prerequisite to receiving services, goods, or both.</skos:definition>
		<skos:inScheme rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/CEDStandards/terms/C001353" />
		<skos:notation>191</skos:notation>
		<skos:prefLabel>Deposits</skos:prefLabel>
	</owl:NamedIndividual>
	<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="https://w3id.org/CEDStandards/terms/NI001353117355">
		<dc:creator>Common Education Data Standards</dc:creator>
		<dc:description>Bond insurance costs that are a form of prepayment to be amortized.</dc:description>
		<dc:identifier rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#token">NI001353117355</dc:identifier>
		<rdf:type rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/CEDStandards/terms/C001353" />
		<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept" />
		<rdfs:label>Bond Insurance Costs</rdfs:label>
		<skos:definition>Bond insurance costs that are a form of prepayment to be amortized.</skos:definition>
		<skos:inScheme rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/CEDStandards/terms/C001353" />
		<skos:notation>193</skos:notation>
		<skos:prefLabel>Bond Insurance Costs</skos:prefLabel>
	</owl:NamedIndividual>
	<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="https://w3id.org/CEDStandards/terms/NI001353117356">
		<dc:creator>Common Education Data Standards</dc:creator>
		<dc:description>Represents amounts to be amortized as debt premium/discount in connection with the issuance of bonds.</dc:description>
		<dc:identifier rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#token">NI001353117356</dc:identifier>
		<rdf:type rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/CEDStandards/terms/C001353" />
		<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept" />
		<rdfs:label>Premium and Discount on Issuance of Bonds</rdfs:label>
		<skos:definition>Represents amounts to be amortized as debt premium/discount in connection with the issuance of bonds.</skos:definition>
		<skos:inScheme rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/CEDStandards/terms/C001353" />
		<skos:notation>194</skos:notation>
		<skos:prefLabel>Premium and Discount on Issuance of Bonds</skos:prefLabel>
	</owl:NamedIndividual>
	<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="https://w3id.org/CEDStandards/terms/NI001353117357">
		<dc:creator>Common Education Data Standards</dc:creator>
		<dc:description>Current assets not provided for elsewhere.</dc:description>
		<dc:identifier rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#token">NI001353117357</dc:identifier>
		<rdf:type rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/CEDStandards/terms/C001353" />
		<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept" />
		<rdfs:label>Other Current Assets</rdfs:label>
		<skos:definition>Current assets not provided for elsewhere.</skos:definition>
		<skos:inScheme rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/CEDStandards/terms/C001353" />
		<skos:notation>199</skos:notation>
		<skos:prefLabel>Other Current Assets</skos:prefLabel>
	</owl:NamedIndividual>
	<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="https://w3id.org/CEDStandards/terms/NI001353117358">
		<dc:creator>Common Education Data Standards</dc:creator>
		<dc:description>Those assets that the school district intends to hold or continue to use over a long period of time. Specifically, capital assets include land, improvements to land, easements, buildings and building improvements, vehicles, machinery, equipment, works of art and historical treasures, infrastructure, and all other tangible or intangible assets that are used in operations and that have initial useful lives that extend beyond a single reporting period. This account is used only in proprietary funds, fiduciary funds, and the government-wide financial statements.</dc:description>
		<dc:identifier rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#token">NI001353117358</dc:identifier>
		<rdf:type rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/CEDStandards/terms/C001353" />
		<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept" />
		<rdfs:label>Capital Assets</rdfs:label>
		<skos:definition>Those assets that the school district intends to hold or continue to use over a long period of time. Specifically, capital assets include land, improvements to land, easements, buildings and building improvements, vehicles, machinery, equipment, works of art and historical treasures, infrastructure, and all other tangible or intangible assets that are used in operations and that have initial useful lives that extend beyond a single reporting period. This account is used only in proprietary funds, fiduciary funds, and the government-wide financial statements.</skos:definition>
		<skos:inScheme rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/CEDStandards/terms/C001353" />
		<skos:notation>200</skos:notation>
		<skos:prefLabel>Capital Assets</skos:prefLabel>
	</owl:NamedIndividual>
	<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="https://w3id.org/CEDStandards/terms/NI001353117364">
		<dc:creator>Common Education Data Standards</dc:creator>
		<dc:description>Tangible property of a more or less permanent nature, other than land, buildings, or improvements thereto, that is useful in carrying on operations. Examples are machinery, tools, trucks, cars, buses, computers, purchased software, furniture, and furnishings. Appendix E provides criteria to distinguish whether a purchase is a supply or a piece of machinery or equipment.</dc:description>
		<dc:identifier rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#token">NI001353117364</dc:identifier>
		<rdf:type rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/CEDStandards/terms/C001353" />
		<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept" />
		<rdfs:label>Machinery and Equipment</rdfs:label>
		<skos:definition>Tangible property of a more or less permanent nature, other than land, buildings, or improvements thereto, that is useful in carrying on operations. Examples are machinery, tools, trucks, cars, buses, computers, purchased software, furniture, and furnishings. Appendix E provides criteria to distinguish whether a purchase is a supply or a piece of machinery or equipment.</skos:definition>
		<skos:inScheme rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/CEDStandards/terms/C001353" />
		<skos:notation>241</skos:notation>
		<skos:prefLabel>Machinery and Equipment</skos:prefLabel>
	</owl:NamedIndividual>
	<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="https://w3id.org/CEDStandards/terms/NI001353117359">
		<dc:creator>Common Education Data Standards</dc:creator>
		<dc:description>A capital asset account that reflects the acquisition value of land owned by a school district. If land is purchased, this account includes the purchase price and costs such as legal fees, filling and excavation costs, and other associated improvement costs incurred to put the land in condition for its intended use. If land is acquired by gift, the account reflects its fair value at the time of acquisition. Permanent improvements to land, such as grading and fill, should also be accounted for in this account. Land and land improvements are considered nonexhaustible assets owing to their significantly long expected useful life. Nonexhaustible assets are not to be depreciated. Therefore, assets classified by asset code 211 should result in no depreciation expense.</dc:description>
		<dc:identifier rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#token">NI001353117359</dc:identifier>
		<rdf:type rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/CEDStandards/terms/C001353" />
		<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept" />
		<rdfs:label>Land and Land Improvements</rdfs:label>
		<skos:definition>A capital asset account that reflects the acquisition value of land owned by a school district. If land is purchased, this account includes the purchase price and costs such as legal fees, filling and excavation costs, and other associated improvement costs incurred to put the land in condition for its intended use. If land is acquired by gift, the account reflects its fair value at the time of acquisition. Permanent improvements to land, such as grading and fill, should also be accounted for in this account. Land and land improvements are considered nonexhaustible assets owing to their significantly long expected useful life. Nonexhaustible assets are not to be depreciated. Therefore, assets classified by asset code 211 should result in no depreciation expense.</skos:definition>
		<skos:inScheme rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/CEDStandards/terms/C001353" />
		<skos:notation>211</skos:notation>
		<skos:prefLabel>Land and Land Improvements</skos:prefLabel>
	</owl:NamedIndividual>
	<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="https://w3id.org/CEDStandards/terms/NI001353117360">
		<dc:creator>Common Education Data Standards</dc:creator>
		<dc:description>A capital asset account that reflects the value of nonpermanent improvements to building sites, other than buildings, that add value to land. Examples of such improvements are fences, retaining walls, sidewalks, pavements, gutters, tunnels, and bridges. If the improvements are purchased or constructed, this account contains the purchase or contract price. If improvements are obtained by gift, it reflects the fair value at the time of acquisition. Site improvements are improvements that have a limited useful life. Because these improvements decrease in their value/usefulness over time, it is appropriate to depreciate these assets. Therefore, all capitalized site improvements should be depreciated over their expected useful life.</dc:description>
		<dc:identifier rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#token">NI001353117360</dc:identifier>
		<rdf:type rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/CEDStandards/terms/C001353" />
		<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept" />
		<rdfs:label>Site Improvements</rdfs:label>
		<skos:definition>A capital asset account that reflects the value of nonpermanent improvements to building sites, other than buildings, that add value to land. Examples of such improvements are fences, retaining walls, sidewalks, pavements, gutters, tunnels, and bridges. If the improvements are purchased or constructed, this account contains the purchase or contract price. If improvements are obtained by gift, it reflects the fair value at the time of acquisition. Site improvements are improvements that have a limited useful life. Because these improvements decrease in their value/usefulness over time, it is appropriate to depreciate these assets. Therefore, all capitalized site improvements should be depreciated over their expected useful life.</skos:definition>
		<skos:inScheme rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/CEDStandards/terms/C001353" />
		<skos:notation>221</skos:notation>
		<skos:prefLabel>Site Improvements</skos:prefLabel>
	</owl:NamedIndividual>
	<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="https://w3id.org/CEDStandards/terms/NI001353117361">
		<dc:creator>Common Education Data Standards</dc:creator>
		<dc:description>Accumulated amounts for the depreciation of land improvements.</dc:description>
		<dc:identifier rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#token">NI001353117361</dc:identifier>
		<rdf:type rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/CEDStandards/terms/C001353" />
		<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept" />
		<rdfs:label>Accumulated Depreciation on Site Improvements</rdfs:label>
		<skos:definition>Accumulated amounts for the depreciation of land improvements.</skos:definition>
		<skos:inScheme rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/CEDStandards/terms/C001353" />
		<skos:notation>222</skos:notation>
		<skos:prefLabel>Accumulated Depreciation on Site Improvements</skos:prefLabel>
	</owl:NamedIndividual>
	<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="https://w3id.org/CEDStandards/terms/NI001353117362">
		<dc:creator>Common Education Data Standards</dc:creator>
		<dc:description>A capital asset account that reflects the acquisition value of permanent structures used to house persons and property owned by the school district. If buildings are purchased or constructed, this account includes the purchase or contract price of all permanent buildings and the fixtures attached to and forming a permanent part of such buildings. This account includes all building improvements, including upgrades made to building wiring for technology. If buildings are acquired by gift, the account reflects their fair value at the time of acquisition.</dc:description>
		<dc:identifier rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#token">NI001353117362</dc:identifier>
		<rdf:type rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/CEDStandards/terms/C001353" />
		<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept" />
		<rdfs:label>Buildings and Building Improvements</rdfs:label>
		<skos:definition>A capital asset account that reflects the acquisition value of permanent structures used to house persons and property owned by the school district. If buildings are purchased or constructed, this account includes the purchase or contract price of all permanent buildings and the fixtures attached to and forming a permanent part of such buildings. This account includes all building improvements, including upgrades made to building wiring for technology. If buildings are acquired by gift, the account reflects their fair value at the time of acquisition.</skos:definition>
		<skos:inScheme rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/CEDStandards/terms/C001353" />
		<skos:notation>231</skos:notation>
		<skos:prefLabel>Buildings and Building Improvements</skos:prefLabel>
	</owl:NamedIndividual>
	<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="https://w3id.org/CEDStandards/terms/NI001353117363">
		<dc:creator>Common Education Data Standards</dc:creator>
		<dc:description>Accumulated amounts for the depreciation of buildings and building improvements.</dc:description>
		<dc:identifier rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#token">NI001353117363</dc:identifier>
		<rdf:type rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/CEDStandards/terms/C001353" />
		<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept" />
		<rdfs:label>Accumulated Depreciation on Buildings and Building Improvements</rdfs:label>
		<skos:definition>Accumulated amounts for the depreciation of buildings and building improvements.</skos:definition>
		<skos:inScheme rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/CEDStandards/terms/C001353" />
		<skos:notation>232</skos:notation>
		<skos:prefLabel>Accumulated Depreciation on Buildings and Building Improvements</skos:prefLabel>
	</owl:NamedIndividual>
