		<rdfs:label>Speech�Independent Study</rdfs:label>
		<skos:definition>Speech�Independent Study courses, often conducted with instructors as mentors, allow students to explore particular topics within the field of language arts (emphasizing speech). Independent Study courses may serve as an opportunity for students to expand their expertise in a particular application, to explore a topic in greater detail, or to develop more advanced skills.</skos:definition>
		<skos:inScheme rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/CEDStandards/terms/C001517" />
		<skos:notation>01197</skos:notation>
		<skos:prefLabel>Speech�Independent Study</skos:prefLabel>
	</owl:NamedIndividual>
	<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="https://w3id.org/CEDStandards/terms/NI001517163246">
		<dc:creator>Common Education Data Standards</dc:creator>
		<dc:description>Speech�Workplace Experience courses provide work experience in a field related to public speaking and speech. Goals are typically set cooperatively by the student, teacher, and employer (although students are not necessarily paid). These courses may include classroom activities as well, involving further study of the field or discussion regarding experiences that students encounter in the workplace.</dc:description>
		<dc:identifier rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#token">NI001517163246</dc:identifier>
		<rdf:type rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/CEDStandards/terms/C001517" />
		<rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept" />
		<rdfs:label>Speech�Workplace Experience</rdfs:label>
		<skos:definition>Speech�Workplace Experience courses provide work experience in a field related to public speaking and speech. Goals are typically set cooperatively by the student, teacher, and employer (although students are not necessarily paid). These courses may include classroom activities as well, involving further study of the field or discussion regarding experiences that students encounter in the workplace.</skos:definition>
		<skos:inScheme rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/CEDStandards/terms/C001517" />
		<skos:notation>01198</skos:notation>
		<skos:prefLabel>Speech�Workplace Experience</skos:prefLabel>
	</owl:NamedIndividual>
	<owl:NamedIndividual rdf:about="https://w3id.org/CEDStandards/terms/NI001517163248">
		<dc:creator>Common Education Data Standards</dc:creator>
		<dc:description>English Morphology and Grammar courses involve the study of the English language�its roots and derivations, structure and sentence patterns, dialects, writing and spelling systems, and uses as a communication tool.</dc:description>
		<dc:identifier rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#token">NI001517163248</dc:identifier>
